      "description": "The raised surface with a strong hairline and the one soft shadow, over a scrim.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-dialog\"><h2>블록 축소</h2><p>얼마나 줄일까요?</p><div class=\"ds-dialog-actions\"><button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-ghost\">취소</button><button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-primary\">미리 보기</button></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-dialog { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; width: min(26rem, 100%); padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid oklch(96% 0.005 150 / 17%); border-radius: 20px; background: oklch(21.5% 0.011 150); box-shadow: 0 18px 48px oklch(4% 0.01 150 / 55%); color: oklch(83% 0.008 150); font-family: 'Pretendard Variable', Pretendard, 'Noto Sans CJK KR', 'Noto Sans KR', system-ui, sans-serif; } .ds-dialog h2 { margin: 0; color: oklch(96% 0.005 150); font-size: 1.375rem; font-weight: 500; } .ds-dialog p { margin: 0; } .ds-dialog-actions { display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 0.5rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid oklch(96% 0.005 150 / 9%); }"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A Calm Dark Dashboard With One Lime Signal",
    "overview": "OhMyDate opens on a dashboard. The ground is near-black with a faint green cast; on it sit a few large cards of related sizes on one grid, with generous dark space between and inside them. Each card says one thing: a small quiet title, one big light number, and a chart or a short list under it. Text is off-white in three steps. Lime is the one signal: the primary button, the current nav item, today, now and next, and the leading series of every chart. Cyan is the second data colour, orange the third; red is kept for danger and overdue. A light scheme shares every token; the theme is the user's choice, dark by default.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black ground with a green cast, three surface steps, hairlines in white at low alpha.",
      "The card is the unit: 20px corners, a hairline edge, a faint top-left sheen in the dark scheme.",
      "One big light number per card (weight 300, tabular), over a small quiet label.",
      "One lime signal; cyan and orange as data; red only for danger and overdue.",
      "Pretendard, bundled; headings medium, body 16px.",
      "Hand-written SVG charts with a text alternative each.",
      "Motion is short and functional; nothing moves under reduced motion.",
      "One glass object, made by this project, in at most one or two places."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Lime Rule",
        "body": "A view has one lime thing to do: its primary button. Lime elsewhere on the view is not an action: the current nav item, the bar of today, the leading series, a \"now\" mark. Lime never means ok, caution or information; those are green, amber and sky."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fill Or Text Rule",
        "body": "A bright hue is either a fill with dark text on it (`--x` under `--color-on-accent`) or text on a surface (`--x-text`). Never `--x` as text in the light scheme, never light text on a bright fill."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Danger Rule",
        "body": "Red is danger and overdue. A deadline is an orange flag; red arrives when it has passed."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Second Signal Rule",
        "body": "No meaning rides on hue alone. A state is a word in its tag; the selected segment is lifted and heavier; a switch moves its knob; the current nav item carries `aria-current`; the numbers of a chart are also text."
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Face Rule",
        "body": "One family. A new role is a size and a weight from the scale. Mono is for code only."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Light Numeral Rule",
        "body": "A number that leads a card is light and large; it is never bold. Times, durations and counts are tabular so they line up."
      },
      {
        "name": "The Whole Word Rule",
        "body": "Hangul words do not break mid-word (`word-break: keep-all`); long ids and URLs may wrap anywhere. Headings balance their lines."
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Glow Rule",
        "body": "No drop shadow on a card, no glow behind a number, no gradient text, no blur on an ordinary card. The only gradient fill is the current nav item and the brand tile."
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour, size, edge and duration from `src/styles/tokens.css`.",
      "Do compose a screen from cards of related sizes on the 12-column grid, with one big light number per card.",
      "Do give every card a title and, where another screen owns the detail, the open icon-link.",
      "Do keep one lime-filled button per view or dialog; other actions are secondary or ghost.",
      "Do compute every number from the user's real data, and show a real empty state when there is none.",
      "Do set text on a bright hue fill in `--color-on-accent`, and use `--x-text` for a hue as text.",
      "Do give every chart a text alternative and every colour-coded mark a second signal.",
      "Do check any new text, tag or mark pair in both schemes before adding a token.",
      "Do keep controls at 44px or more on coarse pointers and the focus ring visible."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add a drop shadow, a glow, gradient text or a blur to an ordinary card.",
      "Don't use lime for ok, caution or information, or red for anything but danger and overdue.",
      "Don't set lime (or any bright hue) as text on a light surface.",
      "Don't read `prefers-color-scheme` in a stylesheet; key on `data-scheme`.",
      "Don't invent a metric, a placeholder statistic or a decorative count-up.",
      "Don't add a chart, icon or 3D library, or fetch a font or image from the network.",
      "Don't set a size or weight outside the scale, or set text in capitals.",
      "Don't animate a layout property, or anything that is not a change of state.",
      "Don't bring in a name, logo, wording, image or exact screen from another product."
    ]
  }
}
